  contentsAnswer: A broken music-box mechanism. My mother wants it playing again
    before Sunday.
  weightAnswer: About eight kilos in the case. The wooden housing is packed separately.
  metalAnswer: Brass gears and a steel spring. Quite a lot of metal.
  packingAnswer: It is on its suspension and still wound. I could not safely release
    the spring.
  responseAnswer: A tap can wake the mechanism a moment later. It pulls back, then
    rattles for a few seconds.
  authorReasoning: 'Innocent delayed counter-motion: 7.8 kg, strong metal, disclosed
    wound mechanism predict the delayed sustained pulse. Delay is not a universal
    Mimic clue.'
